index 2002795..b3035ef 100644
--- a/docs/management/api.md
+++ b/docs/management/api.md
@@ -3204,6 +3204,14 @@ Top-level response fields:
 | `top` | object | `users`, `client_keys`, `credentials`, `providers`, `models`, `endpoints`, and `errors`. |
 | `activity` | array | Health activity series aligned one-for-one with the contiguous trend buckets. `status` is `empty` for zero requests, `healthy` below 5% errors, `degraded` from 5% to below 50% errors, and `unavailable` from 50% errors. |
 
+### Incremental usage summaries
+
+`GET /usage/summary-records` requires `from` and `to` (`[from,to)`), accepts `limit` up to 200, and returns narrow `items` with string IDs, exact timestamps, provider/model, tokens and token breakdown, client username, credential ID, and billing amount/rule. Diagnostics, raw keys, credential JSON, request content and balances are omitted. Continue with both `after_timestamp` and string `after_id` from `next`; order is timestamp then ID, ascending. `next: null` completes that fixed range. Requires `usage_summary_cursor_v1`.
+
+`GET /usage/summary-pending?to=<RFC3339>` returns up to 200 pending items with `pending_token` and `more`. Inserts and attribution repairs queue IDs in the source transaction, including late commits behind any cursor. Future timestamps remain queued until `to` passes them. Commit counters and deduplication receipts durably before `POST /usage/summary-ack` with `{"items":[{"id":"123","token":"<observed pending_token>"}]}`. At most 200 pairs; replay is safe. Only the observed token is removed, so a concurrent repair remains pending. There is one summary consumer per Home; this is not a broadcast feed. Requires `usage_summary_pending_v1`.
+
+`GET /usage/first-success` requires positive `client_key_id`, `from`, and repeated `credential_id` values (at most 500). Returns the earliest successful timestamp at or after `from`, restricted to those canonical credentials and the charged key (falling back to legacy key identity only when no charged key exists). Empty credentials or no match returns `{"timestamp":null}`. Requires `usage_first_success_v1`.
+
 ### GET `/usage/records`
 
 Returns the request record table with server-side pagination, filters, and sorting.
